## APM Workflow

> Canonical reference: [`.cursor/skills/project-initialization/references/apm-workflow.md`](mdc:../skills/project-initialization/references/apm-workflow.md). The rule below summarises the workflow; every operational detail (CLI install commands, registry URLs, hook contracts, troubleshooting matrix) lives in that doc.

- Every initializer / updater flow runs a **Phase 0** gate that verifies the APM CLI is installed (`apm --version`) and walks the user through `curl`/`irm`/`brew`/`pip` install if missing.
- The canonical packages catalogue lives in the standalone [Workplace-Agent-Packages](https://git.netcracker.com/DEMO.SE.AI/Workplace-Agent-Packages) repo (`.core-version.json → apmPackages.registryRepoUrl`). Each top-level directory is an installable APM package. Consumers reference them as object-form deps: `git: <registryRepoUrl>`, `path: <id>`, `ref: <git-ref>`.
- `/initialize` Phase 1.7-APM fetches the registry `index.json` (built-in / external URL / both), filters by selected role(s), writes the project's `apm.yml`, and runs `APM_LEGACY_SKILL_PATHS=1 apm install`. The flag is mandatory — it preserves the `.cursor/skills/<name>/` deploy path required by Phase 6 Part 3.5.
- **`apm install` reporting success is not evidence that packages landed with content.** APM judges freshness from the `apm.lock.yaml` entry, so an entry poisoned by an earlier interrupted run (`version: unknown`, `package_type` other than `apm_package`, or `content_hash: sha256:e3b0c442…b855` — the hash of empty input) makes every later install print `(files unchanged)` and re-materialise nothing; the package stays an empty directory skeleton that passes existence checks. Run `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .cursor/skills/project-initialization/scripts/validate-apm-install.ps1` on **both** sides of the install — Phase 1.7-APM step 5.0b with `-PreInstall` (inherited state only) and step 5.1a without it (full gate) — and treat exit 1 as a stop. Purge the cached tree plus the lock entry as the script instructs; never hand-create files inside a package-owned skill. Cause and remediation: [`apm-workflow.md`](mdc:../skills/project-initialization/references/apm-workflow.md) §5 (Lockfile). Every `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File …` command in this template means "`pwsh -File …` where `pwsh` resolves, otherwise this" — see [`environment-setup.md`](mdc:../skills/project-initialization/references/environment-setup.md); where no PowerShell exists at all, record the gate as an Open Gap rather than declaring it passed.
- Full modules ship `scripts/activate.{sh,ps1}` plus a `SessionStart` descriptor in `.apm/hooks/activate.json`. On APM 0.28.0 the descriptor IS copied into `.cursor/hooks.json`, but verbatim in the Claude event shape (PascalCase keys, nested `hooks` arrays, unresolved extensionless `${PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/activate`) — Cursor's hooks schema does not execute it, so **`SessionStart` does not effectively fire**. Activate a module by running its `scripts/activate.{sh,ps1}` directly, from the package root that holds both `apm.yml` and `runtime/` — **never** the byte-identical copy APM leaves at `.cursor/hooks/<pkg>/scripts/`, which has no `runtime/` and silently activates nothing while still writing the marker. The script is idempotent via `.workplace/activated/<pkg>.marker`, so that false marker permanently suppresses the correct run: judge activation by the relocated payload, using `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .cursor/skills/project-initialization/scripts/verify-apm-activation.ps1` (`-Repair` to clear false markers). Details: [`apm-workflow.md`](mdc:../skills/project-initialization/references/apm-workflow.md) §6.1–6.2.
- Phase 7 of `/initialize` (AGENTS.md generation) MUST preserve the `<!-- apm:start -->` / `<!-- apm:end -->` pair and everything between them verbatim — that region is owned by `apm compile` (the project's `apm.yml` sets `compilation.agents_md.mode: managed_section`, written by Phase 1.7-APM since template v4.5.0). Phase 7 only edits Workplace-managed sections outside those markers. The pre-v4.5.0 `<!-- APM:<name> begin/end -->` contract is retired — `apm compile` never emitted such markers.
- New packages are authored with `/package-new` (skill: `apm-packaging`) in a clone of the Workplace-Agent-Packages repo. Three source modes: `--from-module <name>`, `--from-skill <name>`, or blank scaffold. Validation gates: `apm compile --validate`, `apm pack --dry-run`, and that repo's `scripts/regenerate-index.ps1` for `index.json` sync.
- The legacy `/moduleActivate` command, `module-activation` skill, `Modules_Registry/` directory, `.cursor/modules/`, and `.cursor/rules/role-packs-state.json` were removed in template v4.0.0.
- `/quick-init` runs a graceful Phase 0 variant (a missing/uninstallable APM CLI never blocks the workflow) and, in its Step 4.5, offers two groups in one batched multi-select: role-agnostic packages — every catalogue entry with empty `targetRoles`, computed at runtime from the freshly resolved registry index (live HTTPS → git → offline snapshot), never from a template-embedded list — and, per its Step 4.5.b.1, the owning package of each domain the stack scan **detected**, labelled with the evidence (detection is not role selection; a declined package is a logged gap). Accepted packages are written to `apm.yml` (dict form, merged by `alias`) and installed with `APM_LEGACY_SKILL_PATHS=1 apm install`. Details: `.cursor/skills/project-initialization/references/quick-init.md` Steps 0 and 4.5.

