## Project Adaptation

Project-specific behavior is configured through three native channels (no parallel "customization" system):

1. **APM package artifacts after install** — files in `.cursor/agents/`, `.cursor/commands/`, `.cursor/skills/` deployed by `apm install` are project-owned relative to the Core and survive `/update-workplace` (they are not listed in `.cursor/rules/.core-version.json` `coreFiles`). Edit them in place to tune agent behavior, command steps, or skill instructions. **APM itself still owns those paths:** `apm install` / `apm update` redeploy them, there is no per-file conflict prompt (collisions land in a diagnostic summary; `--force` overwrites outright), and `apm audit` reports hand-edits as `modified` drift. For an edit that must survive package refreshes, keep the customized copy in the project's own `.apm/` directory (`.apm/agents/<name>.agent.md`, `.apm/skills/<name>/`, `.apm/prompts/<name>.prompt.md`) — local primitives are deployed last and win on collision. Every manual `apm install`/`apm update` needs `APM_LEGACY_SKILL_PATHS=1`.
2. **`AGENTS.md` "Project Conventions" section** — the root `AGENTS.md` file is auto-loaded by Cursor on every conversation. Place team-wide rules, repository conventions, and pointers to project tooling in its `Project Conventions` section. Reference role-pack skills via their `references/guidelines.md` instead of duplicating their content.
3. **`project-config.json` + `references/guidelines.md`** per context skill (`coding-standards-context`, `infrastructure-context`, and any role-pack `*-context` skill) — machine- and human-readable domain settings filled during initialization Phase 6. Edit `project-config.json` and regenerate `references/guidelines.md` to change domain-specific behavior.

> The legacy `project-*` prefix convention (`project-*` agents/commands/skills) and `.cursor/rules/project/*.mdc` rule files were removed in v3.0.0. Existing `project-*` artifacts are detected and migrated by `/update-workplace` (see `migration_v3_0_drop_project_customizations` in `.cursor/skills/project-update/references/migration-and-scan.md`). Only `.cursor/rules/project/metadata.json` remains in that directory. Full guide: [docs/core/CUSTOMIZATION.md](https://git.netcracker.com/DEMO.SE.AI/nc-ai-workplace/-/blob/master/docs/core/CUSTOMIZATION.md).

